# Auto-load the pinned dev shell on `cd` into the repo, so bare
# `zig build test` works without typing `devenv shell`.
#
# One-time setup: install direnv (https://direnv.net) and devenv
# (https://devenv.sh/getting-started/), then run `direnv allow` here.
# Without devenv this file says so and gets out of the way rather than
# failing the `cd`.
#
# The pin is not decoration. build.zig.zon requires Zig 0.16, and four
# of the six gates in CLAUDE.md shell out to tools Zig does not bring —
# the real `openssl` binary, a Go toolchain, a python3, and git for the
# two pinned checkouts. Each of those gates degrades to a readable SKIP
# when its tool is missing, which is exactly the failure mode a shared
# shell is for: a SKIP is not a failure, so an incomplete toolchain turns
# gates off quietly. devenv.nix supplies all four so it cannot.
#
# `zig build tlsanvil` is the exception it cannot close: TLS-Anvil ships
# as a container, and a reachable Docker daemon is not something a shell
# can put on PATH. devenv.nix says why it does not try.
#
# There is no `use flake` fallback: zssl carries no flake.nix, unlike the
# sibling zoxy checkout, and `use flake` against a missing flake fails
# the `cd` instead of degrading.
if has devenv; then
  eval "$(devenv direnvrc)"
  use devenv
else
  echo "zssl: devenv not found — see CLAUDE.md for the toolchain the gates need" >&2
fi
